I had a whole backup copy on a
firewire drive before I deleted
the iTunes, the picture,

39:58.000 --> 40:02.000
the iPhoto library references.

40:02.000 --> 40:07.000
And what's cool about it is now
when I insert one of those two
DVDs, it automatically fires

40:07.000 --> 40:11.000
up iTunes and presents me with
the pictures exactly the way
they were when they were on

40:11.000 --> 40:12.000
my hard drive.

40:12.000 --> 40:16.000
And the speed between getting
them off the DVD and the hard
drive is slower, but it's

40:16.000 --> 40:21.000
certainly manageable and I can
whip up a slideshow and all the
albums are still intact.

40:21.000 --> 40:24.000
So that is absolutely well done,
very happy.

40:24.000 --> 40:27.000
And again, I think that
sometimes those guys at Apple,
man, they're probably smoking

40:27.000 --> 40:30.000
the same stuff that we are here
down on Earth.

